# Data Scientist Workflow Rules

## Seed discipline is mandatory

Every experiment sets a random seed before any random operation. There are no exceptions.

Required patterns before any call to `train_test_split`, `np.random.`, `torch.`, `random.`, or similar:

```python
import random, numpy as np
SEED = 42  # document and log this value
random.seed(SEED)
np.random.seed(SEED)
# torch.manual_seed(SEED)      # if using PyTorch
# tf.random.set_seed(SEED)     # if using TensorFlow
```

The `seed-check` hook fires on every `.py` and `.ipynb` edit in `notebooks/` and warns if no seed is found. Treat this warning as an error before handoff.

## No raw data in the repository

Only data paths and content hashes enter the repository. Never commit:
- CSV files
- Parquet files
- Database dumps or exports
- Any file from `data/` that contains actual records

Add `data/` to `.gitignore`. If a dataset must be shared with the team, document its location and provide a reproducible download or query script instead.

## Notebooks run top-to-bottom

Before handoff, every notebook must:
1. Have all outputs cleared
2. Be re-run from top to bottom without errors
3. Have monotonically increasing `execution_count` values (1, 2, 3, ...)

The `notebook-lint` hook fires on every `.ipynb` edit and warns if cells appear unexecuted. The `reproducibility-checker` agent verifies execution order before `/ds-validate` completes.

## Experiments are logged

No experiment result exists only in your memory or a notebook output cell. After every experiment run:

- Invoke `experiment-tracker` to append a row to `docs/experiments/log.md`
- The row must include: timestamp, seed, model config, train metrics, validation metrics, artifact paths

The `log-experiment` hook fires at session end to remind you if this step was skipped.

## Model card required for handoff

No handoff occurs without a completed model card. `/ds-handoff` enforces this checklist:

- [ ] Model card written (`docs/model-card-{name}.md`)
- [ ] Validation passed (`docs/validation-{model}.md`)
- [ ] Reproducibility confirmed (all `reproducibility-checker` checks pass)
- [ ] Model artifact saved in `artifacts/`
- [ ] Experiment log up to date

## Subagent delegation

Delegate to subagents at these workflow transitions:

| When | Delegate to |
|---|---|
| New dataset available | `data-profiler` → produces `docs/profile-{dataset}.md` |
| Experiment run complete | `experiment-tracker` → appends to `docs/experiments/log.md` |
| Before `/ds-validate` handoff step | `reproducibility-checker` → verifies seed, deps, paths, execution order |
